[{"sha":"fa3fea8260d41fe25964af8119e65d151c4841c5","node_id":"C_kwDOEQlWGtoAKGZhM2ZlYTgyNjBkNDFmZTI1OTY0YWY4MTE5ZTY1ZDE1MWM0ODQxYzU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Sebastian Calonico","email":"scalonico@ucdavis.edu","date":"2026-10-06T02:56:08Z"},"committer":{"name":"Sebastian Calonico","email":"scalonico@ucdavis.edu","date":"2026-10-06T02:56:08Z"},"message":"Address the independent review of PR #25\n\n- Python: negative weights raise ValueError in rdrobust() and rdbwselect(),\n  as the CHANGELOG states (they raised a bare Exception).\n- Python: a single cluster on a side gives NaN standard errors, as in R,\n  instead of a ZeroDivisionError in the CR1 factor g/(g-1).\n- Stata: a non-numeric nnmatch token in vce(nn ...) exits 125 with a message\n  (vce(nn cl) used to die inside Mata with \"cl not found\"); rdrobust and\n  rdbwselect.\n- CHANGELOG: scope the row-order statement for ginv.tol to the verified case\n  (Kuo data, default options); the hc*/masspoints(\"off\") path keeps a ~1e-3\n  dependence in near-collinear designs, as in 4.0.0. Entries for the two\n  fixes above.\n- Python tests: expect ValueError; new single-cluster test (57 pass).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"994f300fedc5fc3dc01b90fefc3b656d526966de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rdpackages/rdrobust/git/trees/994f300fedc5fc3dc01b90fefc3b656d526966de"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rdpackages/rdrobust/git/commits/fa3fea8260d41fe25964af8119e65d151c4841c5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rdpackages/rdrobust/commits/fa3fea8260d41fe25964af8119e65d151c4841c5","html_url":"https://github.com/rdpackages/rdrobust/commit/fa3fea8260d41fe25964af8119e65d151c4841c5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rdpackages/rdrobust/commits/fa3fea8260d41fe25964af8119e65d151c4841c5/comments","author":{"login":"scalonico","id":29930933,"node